      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1912 a wooden Methodist church burned, prompting the construction of a brick Gothic‑Revival church across the railroad tracks in 1913.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://carrollcountyhistory.org/whitesburg.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The McIntosh Reserve, a 527‑acre park on the Chattahoochee River, is named after Creek leader William McIntosh Jr.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
